SUMMARY:Summer Reading Kick-off at North Regional Library
DESCRIPTION:Ready\, set\, Read! Stop by North Regional Library on 
 Saturday\, June 13\, 2026\, between 10 a.m. - Noon for a fun celebration to 
 kick off Durham County Library's Summer Reading Program. This year's Summer 
 Reading runs from June 15\, 2026- August 8\, 2026\, and is themed: " 
 Unearth a Story." \n\nCome enjoy dinosaur-themed activity stations for all 
 ages (indoor and outdoor)\, free concessions\, and connect with community 
 partners. Learn more about the exciting events we have planned this 
 summer\, and don't forget to pick up your reading log and a free book (for 
 children and teens\, while supplies last). This program will be held at 
 North Regional Library. The address is 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712. 
 \n\nThis program is brought to you by the generous support of the Durham 
 Library Foundation. \n\nQuestions? Please email Molly at 
 mschaefer@dconc.gov or call 919-560-0236. Thank you!
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:High & Low Sensory Stimulation, Summer Reading
