SUMMARY:Water Features from Bird Baths to Ponds
DESCRIPTION:Join us to learn why and how to add a water feature to your 
 garden\n\nPresented by Sheldon Galloway\, Owner and Head of Operations at 
 Garden Environments\n\nLandscape water features are a feast for the eyes\, 
 and the sound of water cascading from a fountain or waterfall can be quite 
 relaxing. The class will talk about types of water features and the 
 benefits of adding one to your garden.\n\nThis class is part of the Hattie 
 Meadows Gardening School and is open to everyone.\n\nThe Hattie Meadows 
 Gardening School is a free community learning project to spread knowledge 
 and love of gardening. Classes will take place at the Stanford L. Warren 
 Library from January through June 2026. This program is presented in 
 partnership with Stanford L. Warren Library\, Sarah P. Duke Gardens\, and 
 Durham County Cooperative Extension\, and is made possible by the Durham 
 Library Foundation.\n\n\n\nRegistration is appreciated to receive an email 
 reminder\, cancellation link\, and program updates. Seating is first come 
 first served. Registration does not hold or guarantee a seat.
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Full Room\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carter Cue":MAILTO:ccue@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-15785122
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15785122
END:VEVENT
