BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260613T180000Z
DTEND:20260613T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260613T000000Z
SUMMARY:Durham Grown: The Durham County Library Garden Club
DESCRIPTION:Tree Pruning Basics!\n\nTrees require pruning to have good 
 structure and thrive in your landscape.There are many considerations that 
 make it necessary to prune trees\, such as safety\, clearance\, and 
 compatibility with your landscape. What is the best time of year to prune? 
 How do you make the correct cuts? What tools are the best for the job? Join 
 Tim Wright\, Master Arborist\, to learn the proper techniques and tools for 
 pruning your trees to protect the cornerstone of your garden!  \n\n\n\nTim 
 Wright is a Board-Certified Master Arborist from Wright Brothers' Tree 
 Service. He is a local expert in tree health care and tree risk management. 
   \n\n\n\nSaturday June 13th starting at 2 p.m. in the auditorium of the 
 Durham County Main Library located at 300 North Roxboro Street in Durham.  
 \n\n \n\nRegistration is appreciated for email reminders\, cancellation 
 links\, and program updates.   \n\n \n\nParking is available in the library 
 lot or at the North Queen Street Garage which is locate at 115 North Queen 
 Street which is located directly across the street from the library. 
 Parking is free in the garage. Bring your parking ticket to a library 
 service point for validation.   \n\n \n\nImage description: A lithograph 
 from 1816 by Antoine-Pierre Mongin titled “Oak Tree (Chene)” of an oak 
 tree growing on the bank of a creek.  \n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham, Environmental, Gardening, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16646252
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16646252
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260613T190000Z
DTEND:20260613T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260613T000000Z
SUMMARY:Summer Reading Kickoff: Multi-Sensory Environment Open House
DESCRIPTION:Check out Main Library's Multi-Sensory Environment! Drop in\, 
 try out the equipment\, and learn more about what our sensory space 
 offers.\n\nThe Multi Sensory Environment provides immersive\, interactive 
 experiences through sight\, sound\, touch\, and smell. The room can be used 
 for play\, therapy\, or teaching\, and sound and light are adjustable to 
 meet visitor needs. All ages welcome!\n\n(The Multi-Sensory Environment is 
 located on the 4th Floor at Main Library.)
