DTSTART:20260616T220000Z
DTEND:20260616T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260616T000000Z
SUMMARY:Wearing Words: A Mask-Making & Poetry Workshop
DESCRIPTION:\nJoin author and poet Khalisa Rae in her Inspired Writer 
 Series with Durham County Library!\n\n\nInspired by Paul Laurence 
 Dunbar’s “We Wear the Mask”\n\n\n\nWhat masks do we wear to 
 survive?\nWho are we underneath them?\n\nInspired by Paul Laurence 
 Dunbar’s iconic poem “We Wear the Mask\,” this workshop invites 
 participants to explore the emotional\, social\, cultural\, and personal 
 masks they wear every day. Through guided discussion\, collage\, 
 reflection\, and poetry writing\, participants will create both a physical 
 “mask” and a written piece that explores the tension between what we 
 reveal and what we hide.\n\nThis workshop centers honesty\, creativity\, 
 softness\, and radical self-expression. Participants do not need prior 
 poetry experience—just a willingness to reflect and 
 create.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNext session is "So You Want to be a Published 
 Writer?" on June 23\, 2026 at East Regional Library.\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ciera Williams":MAILTO:cbwilliams@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Durham, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16970125
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16970125
END:VEVENT
