SUMMARY:Day 2 – Water\, Soil\, Crops\, High Tunnel Agriculture & Animal Production
DESCRIPTION:Free NC A&T & PHIRST® workshop series. Attend 1 day\, multiple 
 days\, or all 4: business\, agriculture\, technology & future 
 farming.\n\nPHIRST® PovertyZero™ Farms & Food Workshop Series with NC 
 A&T\n\nJoin North Carolina A&T State University and PHIRST® for a free 
 four-day workshop series focused on certification pathways\, sustainable 
 agriculture\, practical skills\, enterprise development\, and applied 
 learning. Participants may attend one day\, multiple days\, or the full 
 four-day series.\n\nThe workshop series is designed for farmers\, future 
 farmers\, backyard growers\, entrepreneurs\, educators\, students\, and 
 community leaders seeking practical knowledge\, certification 
 opportunities\, hands-on experience\, and sustainable enterprise 
 strategies.\n\nDAY 2 – WATER\, SOIL\, CROPS\, HIGH TUNNEL AGRICULTURE & 
 ANIMAL PRODUCTION\nParticipants learn about soil and water management\, the 
 hydrologic cycle\, irrigation systems\, high tunnel agriculture\, soil 
 properties\, specialty crop production\, fertigation\, small-ruminant 
 production\, animal health\, feeding practices\, and productivity 
 management. This day focuses on improving production efficiency\, 
 sustainability\, and farm profitability.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL GAIN\n Practical 
 agricultural knowledge and skills\n Sustainable farming and enterprise 
 strategies\n Certification opportunities through NC A&T OPPE pathways\n 
 Exposure to innovative technologies and systems\n Networking with 
 agricultural professionals\, educators\, entrepreneurs\, and community 
 leaders\n Real-world examples of scalable agricultural 
 enterprises\n\nAttendance is free\, but registration is required.\nSeating 
 is limited to 150 participants per day. \n\nREGISTER ON EVENTBRITE 
 HERE\n\nThere will be no live animals at this event.   \n\nParking is 
 available in the library parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage 
 located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the apartments directly 
 across the street from the library. Parking at the garage is free. Please 
 bring your parking ticket to a service point for validation.       
 \n\nAttend one day\, multiple days\, or the entire four-day 
 series.\n\nLearn. Grow. Innovate. Build Sustainably.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17056753
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17056753
END:VEVENT
