DTEND:20260625T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260625T000000Z
SUMMARY:DAY 4 – Integrated Enterprise Systems Practicum
DESCRIPTION:Free NC A&T & PHIRST® workshop series. Attend 1 day\, multiple 
 days\, or all 4: business\, agriculture\, technology & future 
 farming.\n\nPHIRST® PovertyZero™ Farms & Food Workshop Series with NC 
 A&T\n\nJoin North Carolina A&T State University and PHIRST® for a free 
 four-day workshop series focused on certification pathways\, sustainable 
 agriculture\, practical skills\, enterprise development\, and applied 
 learning. Participants may attend one day\, multiple days\, or the full 
 four-day series.\n\nThe workshop series is designed for farmers\, future 
 farmers\, backyard growers\, entrepreneurs\, educators\, students\, and 
 community leaders seeking practical knowledge\, certification 
 opportunities\, hands-on experience\, and sustainable enterprise 
 strategies.\n\nParticipants experience the future of scalable small-farm 
 and community-enterprise systems through demonstrations of integrated 
 solutions for water\, food production\, energy\, sustainability\, and 
 regenerative resource management. The practicum demonstrates how Water 
 Sustainability For LIFE\, Farms and Food\, Applied Sustainable Energy 
 Solutions\, and Sustainable Regenerative Sanitation work together to reduce 
 operating costs and increase production yields. \n\nWHAT YOU WILL GAIN\n 
 Practical agricultural knowledge and skills\n Sustainable farming and 
 enterprise strategies\n Certification opportunities through NC A&T OPPE 
 pathways\n Exposure to innovative technologies and systems\n Networking 
 with agricultural professionals\, educators\, entrepreneurs\, and community 
 leaders\n Real-world examples of scalable agricultural 
 enterprises\n\nAttendance is free\, but registration is required.\nSeating 
 is limited to 150 participants per day. \n\nREGISTER ON EVENTBRITE 
 HERE\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the North 
 Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the 
 apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking at the 
 garage is free. Please bring your parking ticket to a service point for 
 validation.       \n\nAttend one day\, multiple days\, or the entire 
 four-day series.\n\nLearn. Grow. Innovate. Build Sustainably.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17056763
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17056763
END:VEVENT
