SUMMARY:Wednesday Computer Class @ Main
DESCRIPTION:Come join a supportive group environment for self-paced digital 
 skills courses. We'll be using Northstar Digital Literacy\, a free online 
 resource available to all Durham County Library patrons. A library staff 
 member will be present to get you set up and answer questions as each 
 participant moves through online modules on their own at their own pace. 
 Northstar allows you to track your learning progress and earn badges or 
 certificates for completing a course. These classes are best for learners 
 who have at least basic keyboard and mouse skills. Our computer lab has a 
 limited number of laptops for use\, so bringing your own laptop and 
 headphones is encouraged.\n\nComputer and digital skills topics 
 include:\n\n\n	Phone Keyboard Basics & Logging In\n	Basic Computer 
 Skills\n	Internet Basics\n	Using Email\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel\, and PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Social 
 Media\n	Information Literacy\n	Career Search Skills\n	Your Digital 
 Footprint\n	Accessing Telehealth Appointments\n	Cybersecurity 
 Basics\n\n\nThese classes are self-paced and each week participants will 
 choose which lessons they want to complete on their own. You do not need to 
 have come to the first class to attend the following weeks and there is no 
 requirement to commit to all of the classes through August. Register for 
 the weeks that work best for you!\n\nIf you have any questions or 
 accommodation needs\, contact Jimmy McKinnell at jmckinnell@dconc.gov or 
 call 919-560-9940\n\n\nÚnase a un ambiente de apoyo para cursos de 
 habilidades digitales a su propio ritmo. Usaremos Northstar Digital 
 Literacy\, un recurso en línea gratuito que también está disponible en 
 español para todos los usuarios de la Biblioteca del Condado de Durham. Un 
 miembro del personal de la biblioteca estará presente para ayudarle a 
 comenzar y responder sus preguntas mientras cada participante avanza por 
 los módulos en línea de manera individual y a su propio ritmo. Northstar 
 le permite llevar un registro de su progreso y obtener insignias o 
 certificados al completar un curso. Estas clases son ideales para personas 
 que ya cuentan con habilidades básicas de teclado y mouse. Nuestro 
 laboratorio de computación tiene una cantidad limitada de laptops 
 disponibles\, por lo que se recomienda traer su propio laptop y 
 audífonos.\n\nLos temas de computación y habilidades digitales 
 incluyen:\n\n\n	Conceptos básicos del teclado del teléfono e inicio de 
 sesión\n	Habilidades básicas de computación\n	Conceptos básicos de 
 Internet\n	Uso del correo electrónico\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel y PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Redes 
 sociales\n	Alfabetización informacional\n	Habilidades para la búsqueda de 
 empleo\n	Su huella digital\n	Cómo acceder a citas de telesalud\n	Conceptos 
 básicos de ciberseguridad\n\n\nEstas clases son autodirigidas y cada 
 semana los participantes elegirán qué lecciones desean completar por su 
 cuenta. No necesita haber asistido a la primera clase para participar en 
 las siguientes sesiones\, y no es necesario comprometerse a todas las 
 clases hasta agosto. ¡Inscríbase en las semanas que mejor le 
 funcionen!\n\nSi tiene preguntas o necesita alguna adaptación\, 
 comuníquese con Jimmy McKinnell a jmckinnell@dconc.gov o llame al 
 919-560-9940.\n
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17001580
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17001580
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260701T220000Z
DTEND:20260702T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T000000Z
SUMMARY:Meet the Curators Then and Now: To Love and Live Free at Durham County Main Library
DESCRIPTION:As part of the Museum of Durham History's Museum Beyond Walls 
 initiative\, which brings Durham history into community spaces beyond the 
 Museum's home at 500 W. Main Street\, join us for a special opening event 
 celebrating the library extension of To Love and Live Free: The 1986 
 Mayoral Recall Fight and the Origins of Durham Pride. Installed outside the 
 North Carolina Collection on the third floor of the Durham County Main 
 Library\, this exhibit explores the key role that the library and its staff 
 played during the controversies of 1986. At the heart of the display are 
 cases recreating the original 1986 Pride Month exhibit that sparked public 
 debate and became part of a defining moment in Durham's history\, featuring 
 many of the same books\, media\, and materials that appeared four decades 
 ago.\n\nThis special "Meet the Curators Then and Now" program offers 
 visitors a unique opportunity to experience the exhibit through the eyes of 
 two people directly connected to it. Joanne Abel\, one of the librarians 
 (along with Nancy Blood) who helped create the original 1986 display\, and 
 Andrew Nurkin\, curator of To Love and Live Free\, will be on hand to 
 provide an intimate guided walkthrough\, sharing personal perspectives\, 
 historical context\, and behind-the-scenes insights into how this story has 
 been preserved and interpreted over the years. The event is free and open 
 to the public and is part of a larger series of programs accompanying To 
 Love and Live Free through early October\, culminating with Durham Pride. 
 Other events include:\n\n“Another Family Against the Amendment” on June 
 27th at 3pm at the Main Library\, presented by The People’s Alliance\, 
 The People’s Alliance Fund\, The Museum of Durham History\, The North 
 Carolina Collection\, and Durham County Library.\n\nIn addition to the 
 installations at the library and the Museum\, a forthcoming traveling 
 version of the To Love and Live Free exhibit will be available for 
 libraries\, schools\, houses of worship\, and other community spaces 
 interested in hosting this important chapter of Durham's history.
LOCATION:Main Library - History Lounge\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="North Carolina Collection NCC":MAILTO:ncc@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17081009
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17081009
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260702T013000Z
DTEND:20260703T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T000000Z
SUMMARY:Teen Art Contest: Unearth Your Story 2026 - SUBMIT YOUR ENTRY NOW!
DESCRIPTION:Unleash your creativity and tell your story through art! 
 Teens\, 13-18\, are invited to participate in our "Unearth Your Story" Art 
 Contest\, inspired by this year’s Summer Reading theme. Create an 
 original piece that explores identity\, history\, imagination\, or 
 discovery.... what story will you uncover?\n\nPick up free art supplies (if 
 needed and while they last)\, submit your masterpiece \, and compete for 
 exciting prizes. Your art will be on display on the Teen floor of Main 
 Library. Community members will vote for their favorites\, and winning 
 artwork will be win four tickets to The Museum of Life and 
 Science.\n\n\n	Submission Period: June 22 – June 30\n	Public Voting: July 
 5 – July 25\n	Winner Announced: July 27\n\n\nWhen dropping off your 
 artwork\, please make sure to have your name\, age\, and contact info 
 written on the back. \n\nFor more information please email 
 vasmondragon@dconc.gov\n\n\n¡Da rienda suelta a tu creatividad y cuenta tu 
 historia a través del arte! Jóvenes de 13 a 18 años están invitados a 
 participar en nuestro concurso de arte “Descubre tu historia”\, 
 inspirado en el tema de Lectura de Verano de este año. Crea una obra 
 original que explore la identidad\, la historia\, la imaginación o el 
 descubrimiento… ¿qué historia vas a descubrir?\n\nRecoge materiales de 
 arte gratis (si los necesitas y hasta agotar existencias)\, envía tu obra 
 maestra y compite por premios emocionantes. Tu arte será exhibido en el 
 área juvenil de la Biblioteca Principal. Los miembros de la comunidad 
 votarán por sus favoritos\, y la obra ganadora recibirá cuatro entradas 
 para el Museum of Life and Science.\n\n\n	Período de entrega: 22 de junio 
 – 30 de junio\n	Votación pública: 5 de julio – 25 de julio\n	Anuncio 
 del ganador: 27 de julio\n\n\nPara mas information envia un coreo a 
 vasmondragon@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Abigail Mondragon":MAILTO:vasmondragon@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-17108067
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17108067
END:VEVENT
